  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 909.18 False Information",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 909.18 False Information.\n\n(a) False information contained in the application or renewal application by either the driver-applicant or the co-applicant shall be grounds for denying a waiver or for revoking a waiver.\n\n(b) The determination by the commissioner whether a waiver will be denied or revoked because of false information shall be based upon the facts and circumstances of each case.\n\nSource. #8404, eff 8-2-05 (from Saf-C 908.14); ss by #10215, eff 10-25-12; ss by #13684, eff 7-17-23\n\nAPPENDIX A\n\nAPPENDIX B\n\nRule | Material Incorporated | How Material May be Obtained\n\nSaf-C 906.01(c) and Saf-C 907.01(b) | North American Standard Out-of-Service Criteria (April 1, 2023) | Available from the publisher, Commercial Vehicle Safety Alliance 6303 Ivy Lane, Suite 301 Greenbelt, MD 20770 Telephone: 301.830-6143 Fax: 301.830-6144 Purchase Online: https://www.cvsa.org/inspections/inspections/out-of-service-criteria/ Cost: $50.00, plus shipping; members $45.00 plus shipping.\n\nSaf-C 906.01(c) & Saf-C 907.01(b) | North American Standard Out of Service Criteria and Level VI Inspection Procedures for Commercial Vehicles Transporting Transuranics and Highway Route Controlled Quantities of Radioactive Materials as defined in 49 CFR Part 173.403 (April 1, 2022) | Commercial Vehicle Safety Alliance 6303 Ivy Lane, Suite 310 Greenbelt, MD 20770-6319 Tel: 301.830-6143 Fax: 301.830-6144 Available by email request by emailing Carlisle Smith: Carlisle Smith Carlisle.smith@cvsa.org Free of Charge www.cvsa.org",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c900.html"
